+- `before_remove` failure or timeout is logged and ignored by default. With the optional
+  `hooks.before_remove_required: true` extension, missing/failed/timed-out hooks prevent
+  local, recorded-path and remote workspace deletion.

 ### 9.5 Safety Invariants

@@ -2133,7 +2135,8 @@ Unless otherwise noted, Sections 17.1 through 17.7 are `Core Conformance`. Bulle
 - `after_create` hook runs only on new workspace creation
 - `before_run` hook runs before each attempt and failure/timeouts abort the current attempt
 - `after_run` hook runs after each attempt and failure/timeouts are logged and ignored
-- `before_remove` hook runs on cleanup and failures/timeouts are ignored
+- `before_remove` hook runs on cleanup; failures/timeouts are ignored unless
+  `hooks.before_remove_required` is enabled, in which case the workspace is retained
 - Workspace path sanitization, stable original-identifier-hash collision resistance, and root
   containment invariants are enforced before agent launch
 - Identifiers unchanged by sanitization keep their deterministic workspace key; conformance tests
